===Go to the clinic and talk to Natasha{{subst:void|<!--201070301-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Natasha's Clinic|You receive a message from Oleg, who hopes you can visit Natasha and see what she's up to.<br />Every day, she works tirelessly to look after the patients, so Oleg hopes you can offer her some help.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Natasha)
----
:'''Natasha:''' You came at a good time, (Trailblazer), there is something you can help me with.
:'''Natasha:''' According to my patient records, there are a few that haven't come for their follow-up visits. It happens from time to time, but never as regularly as this. I'm a bit concerned...
:'''Natasha:''' Have you heard of the Complex Illness Mutual Aid Society?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Sounds like a charitable organization.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Sounds suspicious...
::'''Natasha:''' Mm, I agree.
:'''Natasha:''' Generally speaking, mutual aid societies like these allow patients to share their experiences and support each other. It's a way of countering all the negative emotional effects of being ill... But there might be more to this society than that.
:'''Natasha:''' I've got a few patients who've started refusing treatment since joining the society... It certainly makes you wonder.
:'''Natasha:''' The most suspicious part is that no matter how much I ask, no one's ever willing to tell me anything about it... and that's where you might be able to help.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Got it, you want me to go undercover.
::'''Natasha:''' ...It sounds dangerous, but what I want you to do is actually very simple. Investigate this so-called "Mutual Aid Society" and find out what exactly they're up to.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Do I need to be ill before I can make inquiries?
::'''Natasha:''' ...That won't be necessary, but it will help if you pretend to be a patient. Help me investigate this so-called "Mutual Aid Society" and find out exactly what they're up to.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What should I do?
::'''Natasha:''' Hmm... Pretend to be a patient. Help me investigate this so-called "Mutual Aid Society" and find out exactly what they're up to.
:'''Natasha:''' If I find out they're preventing me from doing my job... or if they're bringing harm to my patients... I won't just sit on the sidelines.
:'''Natasha:''' Can I entrust you with this task, (Trailblazer)?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} No problem, leave it with me.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Have I ever refused you?
::'''Natasha:''' You're as considerate as always, (Trailblazer).
:'''Natasha:''' This little clinic has huge numbers of patients to deal with every day... If I didn't have you here to help me out, I wouldn't be able to focus on giving them quality care.
:'''Natasha:''' Good luck, (Trailblazer). I'll be sure to thank you properly when you're back.
----
{{Dialogue End}}

===Talk to the first patient who skipped the follow-up visit{{subst:void|<!--201070302-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Boulder Town|update|As the chief of Wildfire and the only doctor in Boulder Town, Natasha is busy every day, and it's almost impossible for her to leave the clinic.<br />What's worse, some stubborn patients refuse to come for a follow-up visit.<br />Do her a favor and persuade the patients who joined the so-called "mutual aid society."}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Depressed Patient)
:'''Depressed Patient:''' You... I've seen you at the clinic. You run errands for Natasha, right?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Well, there goes my cover...
::'''Depressed Patient:''' ...Your cover? What are you talking about?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Uh... Who's Natasha?
::'''Depressed Patient:''' ...Don't play dumb. I might be sick but my eyes still work.
:'''Depressed Patient:''' *sigh* Let me guess, Natasha wants you to persuade me to go back for a follow-up visit, right?
:'''Depressed Patient:''' *sigh* ...What's the use? I'm terminal. Life'll be over before I know it.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Was that Natasha's diagnosis?
:'''Depressed Patient:''' Of course not, I read it in a book.
:'''Depressed Patient:''' Every book I read has descriptions that match my symptoms exactly... I can diagnose myself with a dozen incurable diseases before I get halfway through.
:'''Depressed Patient:''' For people in my situation, a follow-up visit is just a waste of time and money... not to mention medicine.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Are you serious?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} ...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Soooo nothing to do with you joining the mutual aid society then?
::'''Depressed Patient:''' Mutual aid what now? What are you talking about?
:'''Depressed Patient:''' ...What else is there to say. Natasha was seeing me free of charge. She said I could keep a tab running for as long as I liked, then pay it back when I had the opportunity... I guess I'm too proud.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Money's one thing, but life...
::'''Depressed Patient:''' You think I need you to tell me? Don't try and persuade me, I've already thought this through...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Appearances are more important than life, I feel you.
::'''Depressed Patient:''' ...Are you making fun of me? Have at it, you won't change my mind.
:'''Depressed Patient:''' *sigh* ...Dr. Vache never charged me anything either. Natasha's great, but Vache was always my number one...
:{{Диалог}} Who's Dr. Vache?
::'''Depressed Patient:''' Natasha's brother? They both used to practice medicine back in Rivet Town.
::'''Depressed Patient:''' I heard he was a top student from the Overworld medical academy &mdash; Belobog's main hospital wanted him. I've no idea what convinced him to set up down here... a kind heart, maybe.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог}} Free medical care? I don't believe it...
::'''Depressed Patient:''' What do you mean? Dr. Vache was a people's doctor &mdash; he handed out free medicine. He even followed up with detailed questions on how we felt.
::'''Depressed Patient:''' The Underworld is always short on medical resources &mdash; they say that Dr. Vache made all his own medicine himself.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why don't you go to him anymore?
::'''Depressed Patient:''' You think I don't want to? I heard that he... passed away.
::'''Depressed Patient:''' Uh... I should keep my voice down. Don't go telling anyone else about this next bit...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I won't.
::'''Depressed Patient:''' I heard that Natasha had something to do with Dr. Vache's death. They say she was jealous that her brother had stolen her patients, so she...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} And you believe that?
:::'''Depressed Patient:''' Agh, it's just something people were saying... I don't think Dr. Natasha could do something like that.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} It's not impossible...
:::'''Depressed Patient:''' ...Hey, it's just a rumor. Don't take my word for it.
::'''Depressed Patient:''' *sigh* Forget I said anything. Since Dr. Natasha sent you over specially, I'll do her a favor.
::'''Depressed Patient:''' I'll go to the clinic for my follow-up a little later. Bye for now...
{{Dialogue End}}

===Talk to the second patient who skipped the follow-up visit{{subst:void|<!--201070303-->}}===
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Elderly Patient)
:'''Elderly Patient:''' ...What was that? You'll have to be louder! My ears aren't what they used to be &mdash; everything's muffled.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I wanted to ask why you're not going for your follow-up visit.
:'''Elderly Patient:''' Hah? Follow-up visit? Is that what you're asking about?
:'''Elderly Patient:''' *sigh* Natasha's a wonderful girl. She always gives me a thorough checkup...
:'''Elderly Patient:''' But at this age, it's rather a lot to bear. Even if they could cure me, I'm sure I wouldn't be around for long. I don't want to waste anyone's time...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} There's no time wasted where health is concerned, right?
::'''Elderly Patient:''' Not for youngsters like yourself. When you get to my time of life, good health is a bit of a luxury I'm afraid.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You should listen to Dr. Natasha.
::'''Elderly Patient:''' That girl's always trying to get me to take my medicine on time. *sigh* I know her heart's in the right place...
:'''Elderly Patient:''' My husband had the same illness as me, but he never touched the medicine. He wanted to make sure I had enough.
:'''Elderly Patient:''' Then one day, he said he needed to take care of some things at the mine. He never came back...
:'''Elderly Patient:''' He was forever saying he wanted to go before I did. Hehe... Selfish old fool...
:'''Elderly Patient:''' I miss him. Now that he's gone, who cares how long I stick around?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'm sure he's up there caring right now.
::'''Elderly Patient:''' ...Do you think so? Wouldn't he want me to hurry up and join him...?
::'''Elderly Patient:''' Hmph... Kids today don't give up easily.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Dr. Natasha cares.
::'''Elderly Patient:''' ...You're not wrong, I suppose. That girl certainly spares me no effort, but I always feel like I'm a burden to her...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I care.
::'''Elderly Patient:''' You don't give up easily, do you? Still... you're full of kind words.
:'''Elderly Patient:''' Okay, you win. It's off for another follow-up visit with Dr. Natasha, I suppose...
:'''Elderly Patient:''' Mm? Did you want to say something else? My ears are terrible...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Have you heard of the mutual aid society?
:'''Elderly Patient:''' Virtual who?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Mutual aid society!
:'''Elderly Patient:''' Alright, I heard you! Do you have to shout? ...No, I've never heard of any mutual aid society...
:<!--2-second delay-->
:'''(Trailblazer):''' (Avoiding a follow-up visit due to money issues...)
:'''(Trailblazer):''' (I should find another patient to talk to...)
