===Report what you found to Natasha{{subst:void|<!--201070305-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Natasha's Clinic|update|The patients who refuse to come to the clinic for the follow-up visit share their different opinions, and the mystery about a type of "wonder medicine" attracts your attention.<br />But the time spent with Natasha makes you believe that she is a good doctor and a good person, you decide to report what you found to her first.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Natasha)
:'''Natasha:''' ...
:'''Natasha:''' So the mutual aid society found my bro&mdash; ...Vache's research results... and now they're selling this so-called "wonder medicine" to patients...?
:'''Natasha:''' Any organization doing something like that is interested in more than just "mutual aid..."
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} The patients wanted me to keep it a secret from you.
::'''Natasha:''' I'm not surprised. They'll know that I'm completely against them using this "wonder medicine..."
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} The patient said he was willing to take the risk.
::'''Natasha:''' ...As a doctor, I don't accept that &mdash; I'm responsible for their well-being. My attitude towards this "wonder medicine" won't change.
:'''Natasha:''' What Vache left behind is nothing more than reagents and experimental by-products... The word "medicine" doesn't apply here.
:'''Natasha:''' I warned the patients countless times, but it seems like they had their heads in the sand all along... No wonder they kept the mutual aid society a secret from me.
:'''Natasha:''' Thank you, (Trailblazer). Those patients weren't exactly singing my praises &mdash; thank you for having faith in me.
:'''Natasha:''' If you're curious about Vache's wonder medicine, you should ask some of the patients in the clinic... see what they have to say about the effects.
{{Dialogue End}}

===Talk to the patients in the clinic{{subst:void|<!--201070306-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Natasha's Clinic|update|You tell Natasha about the wonder medicine. She states that she's strongly against the mutual aid society selling drugs.<br />Natasha suggests you talk to the patients in her clinic to hear different opinions on the wonder medicine.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Emotional Patient)
:'''Emotional Patient:''' The medicine Vache left behind? That stuff... Can you even call it medicine?
:'''Emotional Patient:''' I know Dr. Natasha's here, but I have to tell it like it is... Vache had zero medical ethics &mdash; he didn't deserve the title "doctor."
:'''Emotional Patient:''' He may have had the capability, but he didn't use it to help anyone... Whenever I went to see him, he never even asked about my illness! He just prescribed me his so-called "wonder medicine..."
:'''Emotional Patient:''' If it were you, would you have taken that medicine?

;(Talk to Calm Patient)
:'''Calm Patient:''' Some people say that Dr. Vache was a saint who came from the Overworld to help those in need... I don't buy it.
:'''Calm Patient:''' "People's doctor..." That's just what people who've bought into the myth like to say. Vache used to distribute free medicine all the time, but, uh... he couldn't have cared less about the people taking the medicine...
:'''Calm Patient:''' The hard truth is that we were just his test subjects. It didn't matter if the medicine worked or not. What mattered was having a constant stream of willing lab rats...
:'''Calm Patient:''' ...Of course, I can't control what anyone else thinks. That's just how I see it.
{{Dialogue End}}

===Talk to Natasha about your thoughts on this matter{{subst:void|<!--201070307-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Natasha's Clinic|update|The patients in the clinic tell you that Dr. Vache, who developed the wonder medicine, doesn't care about his patients at all.<br />This is completely different from what you heard from those who joined the mutual aid society.<br />Perhaps Natasha is the only one who knows the truth... After all, she's Vache's sister.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Natasha)
:'''Natasha:''' ...I still haven't worked out how to convey it to you, the issues surrounding Vache. My relationship with him... the things he's done in the Underworld... it's a long story.
:'''Natasha:''' I'm guessing you've heard a lot of different opinions on Vache. What do you make of him, (Trailblazer)?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I think he was a doctor with zero medical ethics.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} It's tough for me to say.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I think he's insane.
::'''Natasha:''' I see... I can understand that.
:'''Natasha:''' (Trailblazer), I want you to go and visit another patient &mdash; a victim of the wonder medicine... I want you to see the real consequences of abusing that medicine.
:'''Natasha:''' Once you've understood her situation, come back and tell me what you think. After that... I want to ask for your help again.
{{Dialogue End}}

===Find the victim of the "wonder medicine"{{subst:void|<!--201070310-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Boulder Town|update|After talking with you, Natasha hopes that you can go to the underworld to visit the last patient.<br />It is said that she is a victim of Vache's "wonder medicine," which means you need to be extra cautious when talking with her...}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Lonely Woman)
----
:'''Lonely Woman:''' ...
:'''Lonely Woman:''' ...Who are you...?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'm a friend of Dr. Natasha.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'm a... miracle doctor from beyond the sky.
:'''Lonely Woman:''' ...Who? And... who am I?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You haven't introduced yourself yet.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You're one of Dr. Natasha's patients, don't you remember?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} ...
:'''Lonely Woman:''' ...Where's my husband... and where's my child...?
:'''Lonely Woman:''' ...Wh&mdash;Where are they? You... you know where they are, right?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'm afraid not. Are you okay?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Try and stay calm...
:'''Lonely Woman:''' ...You don't know... they don't know... nobody knows...
:'''Lonely Woman:''' Where... Wh&mdash;Where did they go...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} ...
:'''???:''' Come over here, child. It's best to leave that poor lady in peace. Let me explain...
----
:'''Kind Old Lady:''' That poor, poor lady... Both her husband and child became ill and passed away.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} They must have been seriously ill...
::'''Kind Old Lady:''' *sigh* ...Not terribly serious. But they needed to get treatment every now and then, which did impact their livelihood.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} And that made her become like this?
::'''Kind Old Lady:''' Yes... Before her family passed away, she was a carefree young woman.
::'''Kind Old Lady:''' Her husband and child caught a mysterious illness. The symptoms weren't grave, but their livelihood was certainly impacted.
:'''Kind Old Lady:''' In order to try and rid themselves of the ailment once and for all, they bought some kind of "wonder medicine..." Who would've thought their condition would deteriorate so rapidly after they began using it.
:'''Kind Old Lady:''' The two began to suffer terribly, such that death became a blessing... It wasn't long before they departed this world, one after the other.
:'''Kind Old Lady:''' From that moment on, oh she became as you see her now. If Dr. Natasha hadn't taken her under her wing... *sigh* Well it doesn't bear thinking about.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} It just sounds like poison...
::'''Kind Old Lady:''' And yet what more could've been done? They were warned about the medicine. They were told about the risks... They chose to roll the dice.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} They were unlucky...
::'''Kind Old Lady:''' Just unlucky? As far as I'm concerned, those medicine dealers are making money for murder in broad daylight... Who would sell such a thing to the sick?
:'''Kind Old Lady:''' *sigh* Talking about it tires me out. At least my husband and I are able to help her where we can. I just hope that one day she can lead a normal life again...
----
{{Dialogue End}}

===Talk to Natasha{{subst:void|<!--201070311-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Natasha's Clinic|update|Vache's wonder medicine destroyed that poor woman's family.<br />Now, you're sure that the so-called Mutual Aid Society is an evil organization that sells counterfeit drugs which can kill people.<br />Go find Natasha again and see what she thinks should be done.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Natasha)
----
:'''Natasha:''' Did you speak to her, (Trailblazer)?
:'''Natasha:''' By the look on your face... I'm assuming you've come to understand the wonder medicine all too well.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} The people selling that stuff are devils.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Those medicine dealers prey on our weaknesses...
:'''Natasha:''' ...
:'''Natasha:''' Be it Vache or the mutual aid society &mdash; forces like that can take full advantage of the... the typical Underworld state of mind.
:'''Natasha:''' Let me tell you a story, (Trailblazer).
:'''Natasha:''' There was once a brilliant Overworld doctor with unmatched pharmaceutical skill.
:'''Natasha:''' The doctor was set on developing a medicine that would steel the human body against the cold. He named his research project "Blizzard Immunity."
:'''Natasha:''' But his research met with obstruction time and time again, the biggest factor being a lack of test subjects. Tampering with the human immune system carries huge risk, and nobody in the Overworld was willing to submit themselves to such experiments.
:'''Natasha:''' As such, the doctor got in touch with his sister in the Underworld... claiming that he wanted to support the medical effort below ground.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} ...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} And then...
:'''Natasha:''' ...Naturally, his sister was overjoyed. After all, as far as medicine was concerned, her brother had always been the standard she'd strived to attain.
:'''Natasha:''' She brought her brother underground and entrusted him with her clinic and laboratory...
:'''Natasha:''' ...I think you know what comes next.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'm sorry that I doubted you before...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} It's hard to believe he was your brother...
:'''Natasha:''' Issuing free medicine to the needy was just Vache's way of conducting experiments on his test subjects.
:'''Natasha:''' On some level, his reagents were able to alleviate the patients' suffering... but nothing more. They would forget their pain for a while, and neglect their regular treatment plans...
:'''Natasha:''' The result... patients with mild illness would attribute their recovery to the so-called wonder medicine, while patients with serious illness would quickly deteriorate... and sometimes die.
:'''Natasha:''' I cannot accept that their fate was simply the result of misfortune or risk, (Trailblazer). No true doctor would accept that.
:'''Natasha:''' That's why I want you to help me recover all the wonder medicine. Are you willing to take on this assignment?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Somebody has to do the right thing.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Not my preferred course of action, but...
::'''Natasha:''' ...But it's impossible to sit on the sidelines, right?
:'''Natasha:''' Thank you, (Trailblazer).
:'''Natasha:''' This will be hard for the people that have come to rely on the wonder medicine... but it's up to us to remove this false hope.
:'''Natasha:''' You mustn't hesitate &mdash; recover every last reagent that Vache left behind. I'll take responsibility for the consequences &mdash; don't worry about that.
:'''Natasha:''' Go, (Trailblazer). I'll be waiting for the good news.
----
{{Dialogue End}}

