===Go back to the clinic and talk to Natasha{{subst:void|<!--201070315-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Natasha's Clinic|update|You defeat the president of the mutual aid society and his helpers, stopping them from ripping off and murdering people by selling counterfeit drugs.<br />Natasha shows her appreciation for you and invites you to the clinic again to chat with her.<br />Maybe she will finally tell you the whole story about Vache.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Natasha)
----
:'''Natasha:''' Oh... (Trailblazer), you're here. I apologize, that must have made for uncomfortable viewing.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Are you okay?
::'''Natasha:''' Mm... I'm okay. If I were in his shoes, I may well have had the same reaction. Now I need to focus on treating the patients, and dispelling their doubts.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'd like to straighten out that loudmouth myself!
::'''Natasha:''' Don't let your emotions get the better of you. If I were in his shoes, I might well have had the same reaction. Now I need to focus on treating the patients, and dispelling their doubts.
:'''Natasha:''' ...Let's leave it for now. I'll feel a lot better once I've gotten rid of this mess that Vache left us.
:'''Natasha:''' ...Now's as good a time as any to tell you Vache's whole story.
:'''Natasha:''' If there's anything you want to know, don't hesitate to ask.
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Was he your biological brother?
::'''Natasha:''' No... but I used to think we were so close that we may as well have been...
::'''Natasha:''' I actually grew up in the orphanage. It wasn't until I was adopted by an Overworld family that life changed for me.
::'''Natasha:''' My adoptive mother always saw me as her own flesh and blood, and Vache loved me like a sister... that is, while we were still young.
::'''Natasha:''' My adoptive parents belonged to a prominent medical family &mdash; as kids, we were exposed to all kinds of medical texts. When we were older, both of us got straight into Belobog's medical school. We were on a path into the medical profession.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} What kind of person was Vache?
::'''Natasha:''' He was gentle and introverted. But when it came to work he could be absurdly obsessive... like a completely different person.
::'''Natasha:''' Whenever I made a mistake in an experiment, he'd bite my head off... and then a while later, he'd apologize and comfort me. He was conflicted in that way.
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} So you knew this medicine was his work?
::'''Natasha:''' I didn't know he had leftover reagents in Rivet Town. I was shocked when you told me.
::'''Natasha:''' If you fail to make a clean break with the past, the past creeps up on you...
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Did he...really pass away?
::'''Natasha:''' *sigh* That's a long story... Ever since he was little, Vache had always wanted to develop a medicine called "Blizzard Immunity."
::'''Natasha:''' He saw the human body's vulnerability to cold as a disease, and wanted to cure it so that humanity could survive the Eternal Freeze. If he succeeded, people would be able to leave Belobog and rebuild their homes in the Snow Plains.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Do you share his vision?
:::'''Natasha:''' To be honest, I never understood how he'd achieve that "Blizzard Immunity." But I do admire that vision and perseverance... I always chose to believe him, ever since I was a kid.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} (Brief silence)
:::'''Natasha:''' I do admire his vision and perseverance, even though "Blizzard Immunity" always seemed unachievable to me.
::'''Natasha:''' I knew his research in the Overworld wasn't going well. I used to write to him and ask him to come down and stay with the kids in the orphanage for a while. I thought it might help take his mind off his research.
::'''Natasha:''' But I was too young to know what long-term frustration could do to a person. It changed him in a terrible way...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Changed him...?
::'''Natasha:''' During his stay in the Underworld, he met patients affected by Fragmentum corrosion with mild symptoms. Compared with non-patients, their bodies reacted differently to hot and cold. And that fascinated Vache.
::'''Natasha:''' He began to simulate mild Fragmentum corrosion, thinking that it could lead to breakthroughs in developing Blizzard Immunity.
::'''Natasha:''' Those reagents of his aren't cure-alls for critical illness &mdash; that doesn't exist. Vache made the reagents to mitigate the suffering of his patients in the short term &mdash; a convenient way for him to observe changes in his test subjects.
::'''Natasha:''' But behind my back, he had been doling out the reagents to residents who were kept in the dark. When it finally struck me that something was wrong, his terrible research had already turned him into... into a madman.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} He'd lost his last shred of humanity...
:::'''Natasha:''' Indeed... and it all happened under my nose. How ridiculous &mdash; my judgment was clouded by trust in a loved one...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Did nothing seem strange to you all that time?
:::'''Natasha:''' I trusted Vache with all my heart. Funny, isn't it? And pathetic.
::'''Natasha:''' When his experiments were exposed, I spent a long time with Oleg discussing how to handle the aftermath.
::'''Natasha:''' This was shortly before the Underworld was sealed off &mdash; there were hardly any Silvermane Guards remaining. We spent ages trying to find a way to handle Vache.
::'''Natasha:''' In the end, Oleg suggested that we banish him and permanently deny him access to the Underworld.
::'''Natasha:''' Had his victims found out the truth, Vache would've been torn to pieces by furious Underworlders. I was young and weak at the time &mdash; Oleg must have worried about how I'd react to such a scenario, or he wouldn't have suggested banishment.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Banishment isn't a particularly harsh punishment...
:::'''Natasha:''' *sigh* Looking back, it wasn't. He deserved much worse...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You two did the right thing.
:::'''Natasha:''' ...I hope so. The day I learned the truth was the day I no longer recognized my brother.
::'''Natasha:''' Oleg and I took Vache to the Overworld. He made his final request to us: To take him outside the city to the Snow Plains he'd always wanted to conquer.
::'''Natasha:''' His figure gradually disappeared into the snow curtain... I've been telling myself that Vache is dead ever since.
::'''Natasha:''' Forgive me, (Trailblazer), I'm not good at telling stories. Vache was a terrible brother and a worse doctor... That's all you need to know.
::'''Natasha:''' Let's call it a day. Thank you for cleaning up the mess my brother left behind. Here &mdash; for your trouble.
::----
{{Dialogue End}}

